---
import Presentation from "../../../../components/Presentation.astro";
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a
          href="/courses/eng-design-fab/"
          class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3"
        >
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Session 14: Evaluate &amp; Reflect</h1>
        <p class="text-sn-theme">Unit 2 &mdash; Manufacturing Foundations, Week 4</p>
        <p class="text-sn-theme"><i>(Last session of Manufacturing Foundations)</i></p>
        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <!-- Launch / Concept -->
        <section id="launch">
          <Presentation>
            <section>
              <h2>Session 14</h2>
              <h3 class="text-sn-theme">Evaluate &amp; Reflect</h3>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>You Designed It. You Cut It.</h2>
              <p>Today: does the real part actually match what you modeled?</p>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate>
              <h2>Bring Back the Calipers</h2>
              <p>
                Unit 1, Session 6 &mdash; measuring precisely, and expecting
                natural variation. Same tool, same discipline, real stakes
                this time.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate data-auto-animate-restart>
              <h2>Measure What Actually Matters</h2>
              <ul>
                <li class="fragment">Overall outer dimensions vs. your model</li>
                <li class="fragment">Pocket depth vs. your designed depth</li>
                <li class="fragment">Hole location vs. your designed location</li>
              </ul>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>A Mismatch Isn't a Failed Session</h2>
              <p>
                If a dimension is off, that's real information &mdash;
                diagnose it using everything from Sessions 7&ndash;10, the
                same way Unit 1's Mismatch Activity treated a bad fit as data,
                not failure.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate>
              <h2>Four Weeks, One Thread</h2>
              <p>
                Client communication, materials, safety, CAD, CAM &mdash;
                all of it aimed at one thing: turning a design into a real,
                trustworthy physical object.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate data-auto-animate-restart>
              <h2>Two Things to Remember</h2>
              <p><b class="text-sn-theme">A measured result beats a remembered impression.</b></p>
              <p class="fragment">
                Your Session 13 gut reaction was a start &mdash; today's
                actual measurements are what count.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate>
              <h2>Two Things to Remember</h2>
              <p><b class="text-sn-theme">Everything you just practiced, you'll do again for real.</b></p>
              <p class="fragment">
                Same pipeline, same discipline &mdash; just your own unique
                design, for an actual client, starting next week.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Next Up</h2>
              <p><b class="text-sn-theme">Week 5: The Arcade Cabinet Project begins.</b></p>
              <p class="fragment">
                Your client brief arrives. Everything from these four weeks
                gets spent for real.
              </p>
            </section>
          </Presentation>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Build -->
        <section id="build">
          <h2>Build</h2>

          <h3>Step 1: Measure Your Part</h3>
          <table class="table table-dark table-sm">
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Feature</th><th>Designed</th><th>Measured</th><th>Difference</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>Outer length</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Outer width</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Pocket depth</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Hole location</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Step 2: Inspect for Quality Issues</h3>
          <p>
            Check for tear-out, tab marks not fully cleaned up, or any
            surface roughness. Note anything you find.
          </p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Step 3: Diagnose Any Mismatch</h3>
          <p>
            For any dimension that differs from your design by more than a
            small amount, use Sessions 7&ndash;10's concepts to explain why
            &mdash; offset, step-down, material behavior, or something else.
          </p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Step 4: Unit Recap</h3>
          <p>
            List the five main skills from this 4-week arc: client
            communication, materials (subtractive and additive), CAD, CAM,
            and safety certification. For each, write one sentence on how it
            showed up in your practice build specifically.
          </p>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Checkpoint -->
        <section id="checkpoint">
          <h2>Checkpoint</h2>

          <p>Your submitted evaluation must include:</p>

          <ul>
            <li>Real measured dimensions, not estimates</li>
            <li>A specific diagnosis for any mismatch &mdash; not "it just came out wrong"</li>
            <li>All five Manufacturing Foundations skills named in your recap</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Reflection -->
        <section id="reflection">
          <h2>Reflection</h2>

          <p>Answer the following questions before submitting your work.</p>

          <ol>
            <li>
              Was your part's biggest dimensional difference bigger or
              smaller than you expected? What does that tell you about
              where you should double-check most carefully next time?
            </li>
            <li>
              Of the five Manufacturing Foundations skills, which one do you
              feel least confident applying to a real, higher-stakes project
              starting next week?
            </li>
            <li>
              This is the last reflection before the real client brief
              arrives. What's one thing about your own process you want to
              do differently once the stakes are real?
            </li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Submit -->
        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>Submit your measurement table, your mismatch diagnosis (if any), your unit recap, and your reflection.</p>

          <h1
            class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash"
          >
            Manufacturing Foundations Complete
          </h1>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
